  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\n\nDisturbances will continue to ride the H5 northwestern periphery of \nthe ridge, resulting in continued chances for showers and storms, \nlikely in the evening and overnight periods. The best chances for \nstorms appear to be early Friday morning (50-70%) in northeast \nNebraska and areawide Saturday night into Sunday (50-70%). Some low \nend potential exists that storms could be strong, particularly \nFriday. Storm chances persist into Monday and Tuesday, but remain \nfairly low at less than 30%. Highs on Friday and Saturday remain \nsimilar to Thursday's highs, while cooler temperatures in the 70s \nand 80s arrive for Sunday through Tuesday.",
